# Executive summary

**What to buy.** {{recommended_desc}}. In the base model it reduces the 99.5% one-year economic capital proxy from USD {{gross_ec:,.0f}}m to USD {{ec_net:,.0f}}m, a capital relief of **{{relief_pct:.1%}}**, for an expected net cost of **USD {{net_cost:,.0f}}m a year** (premium USD {{premium:,.0f}}m less expected recoveries of USD {{exp_recovery:,.0f}}m). That is an implied cost of capital of **{{implied_coc:.1%}}**, {{coc_vs_hurdle}} the {{hurdle:.0%}} hurdle assumed for the insurer's own capital.

**Why.** The programme sits on the cost–capital frontier of {{n_programmes}} candidate programmes and is the Balanced choice at a {{hurdle:.0%}} hurdle: every additional step of protection up to it releases capital at a marginal cost below the hurdle, and {{next_step_sentence}}. Equivalently, it minimises the total cost of risk (net reinsurance cost + {{hurdle:.0%}} × net EC): USD {{tcr_rec:,.0f}}m against USD {{tcr_gross:,.0f}}m with no reinsurance and USD {{tcr_budget:,.0f}}m for the cheapest programme that releases at least {{budget_min_relief:.0%}} of capital.

**How much to trust it.** {{stress_sentence}} Two things drive the result and deserve management's attention. First, the reinsurer's diversification: with none (d = 1), reinsurance capital costs more than equity and the same rule picks {{d10_balanced_desc}}. Second, the tail rests on few events: without {{eo_event}} gross EC falls by {{eo_ec_drop:.0%}}, and the year bootstrap gives a 90% interval of {{relief_pct_p05:.0%}}–{{relief_pct_p95:.0%}} for capital relief.

**Affordability.** The recommended programme's premium is {{premium_share_of_portfolio:.0%}} of the portfolio's own premium (USD {{portfolio_premium_m:,.0f}}m). This is large because, at a {{hurdle:.0%}} hurdle, holding the gross capital would cost USD {{tcr_gross:,.0f}}m a year, more than the portfolio's expected margin before expenses (USD {{expected_margin:,.0f}}m). If that premium is not affordable, the Budget-first programme ({{budget_first_desc}}) releases {{budget_relief_pct:.0%}} of capital for USD {{budget_net_cost:,.0f}}m a year.

