# Portfolio and catastrophe model

**Portfolio.** NFIP policies in force in the five Gulf states, written in 2025: {{portfolio_policies:,.0f}} insured units, USD {{portfolio_tiv_bn:,.0f}}bn total insured value ({{fl_tiv_share:.0%}} in Florida) and USD {{portfolio_premium_m:,.0f}}m premium. It is a stylised reference portfolio built from NFIP data, not a model of the NFIP's finances. National totals from the same extract ({{national_policies_2025:,.0f}} insured units, USD {{national_tiv_2025_tn:.2f}}tn) match the order of magnitude published by the Congressional Research Service.

**Events.** Claims ({{claims_rows:,}} in 2009–2025) are grouped by FEMA's `floodEvent` label and each event is restated to 2025 exposure by the ratio of state written insured value in 2025 to the event year (no CPI, which would double count value growth). Events of at least USD {{u0:,.0f}}m as-if form the catalogue: {{n_events_calib}} events in {{calibration_start}}–{{calibration_end}} totalling USD {{calib_event_total_bn:,.1f}}bn; everything else is attritional (mean USD {{attritional_mean:,.0f}}m a year). In the active years one event supplied most of the year's loss, the signature of accumulation risk.

{{tbl_events}}

**Loss model.** Annual loss = attritional + sum of event losses. Frequency is {{frequency_family}} with {{frequency_mean:.2f}} events a year (dispersion index {{dispersion:.2f}}; likelihood-ratio statistic {{lr_stat:.2f}}, far below the {{lr_critical}} needed for a negative binomial). Severity is a {{severity_family}} fitted by maximum likelihood with left truncation at USD {{u0:,.0f}}m, chosen by AIC among lognormal, log-logistic and Burr XII after checking that each of the five largest events is unremarkable under the fit. The three fits are within {{aic_spread:.1f}} AIC points of each other; with only {{n_events_calib}} events, generalised Pareto tail estimates were unstable, so GPD is used only as a stress. Each simulated event is capped at {{cap_multiple:.0f}}× the largest calibration event (USD {{cap:,.0f}}m). Attritional loss is bootstrapped from the calibration years.

**Simulation.** {{n_sims:,}} years (seed {{seed}}); VaR 99.5 moves by {{conv_diff:.2%}} at {{conv_years:,}} years. Gross mean loss USD {{gross_mean:,.0f}}m, 1-in-200 annual loss USD {{gross_var_995:,.0f}}m, EC USD {{gross_ec:,.0f}}m. {{cap_sentence}} The tail beyond the largest observed event therefore comes from the fitted shape and the cap, not from data.

